<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Script-dependent typography, selected by the RESOURCE SYSTEM.

     There must never be an `if (locale == "fa")` in Kotlin, for the same reason
     CLAUDE.md 6b bans `if (brand == ...)`: the moment one exists, every new
     locale is a code change. A qualified resource is the only mechanism that
     scales to 38 of them.

     paywall_letter_tracking gates two things on the paywall:
       * letterSpacing on the eyebrow (3sp) and the savings chip (0.8sp).
         Tracking is inserted BETWEEN letterforms. Arabic-script letters JOIN,
         so tracking pulls a word apart into what reads as a typo.
       * FontFamily.Serif on the headline. Android's fallback stack ships no
         serif Arabic face, so Serif silently degrades to the default sans in
         exactly those locales — better substituted on purpose than by accident.

     false in: ar, fa, fa-rIR, ckb, b+azb (every Arabic-script locale we ship).
     Candidates worth an owner decision, deliberately NOT changed here: my
     (Myanmar), km (Khmer), th (Thai), bo (Tibetan) are complex scripts where
     tracking is also questionable, but they do not join and the failure is
     cosmetic rather than word-breaking. -->
<resources>
    <bool name="paywall_letter_tracking">true</bool>
</resources>
